sentences.l:
I will give to him this sword, all-bronze, on which a hilt
of silver, and a sheath of newly-sawn ivory
has been set round;

And meanwhile Arete for the stranger a very fair chest
brought out of the chamber, and put in it fair gifts,
clothing and gold, which the Phaeacians had given him;

But when this heard much-enduring, heavenly Odysseus,
at once he fitted on the lid, and swiftly upon it cast a fastening
intricate, which once him taught in mind the lady Circe;

“Nausicaa, daughter of great-spirited Alcinous,
so now may Zeus ordain, loud-crashing husband of Hera,
to come home and see the homecoming day;

Then indeed to the herald addressed many-wiled Odysseus,
from the chine cutting off, and more remained over,
of a white-toothed pig, and abundant was the fat on both sides:
